          "Functional": false,
          "Popularity": 74,
          "Donor": "Thomas Osgood Jr.",
          "Accession Date": "2021-03-02",
          "Provenance": "<p>Made at the Osgood Manufacturing Co. in Riverside around 1905. Belonged to three generations of the Osgood family before being donated by the estate executor. Clockwork mechanism seized circa 1935 and was never repaired.</p>",
          "Notes": "<p>Paint loss on the roof consistent with sustained handling. Two wheels are non-original replacements. The <em>No. 14</em> numerals on the cab were probably applied after manufacture by a child owner.</p>"
        }
      },

