          "Functional": false,
          "Popularity": 30,
          "Donor": "Riverside Public School",
          "Accession Date": "2015-08-20",
          "Provenance": {
            ".machine-translate": "Never",
            ".en": "<p>One of three lullabies Arthur Van Bergen transcribed from Mrs. Martha Davies, a parent of one of his students, in March 1898. The manuscript is the only written record of the tune. The words — a mixture of English and nonsense syllables — should be preserved as written.</p>"
          },
          "Notes": "<p>This item demonstrates v1.4-draft polymorphic translatable fields: the <em>Title</em> carries an English and French variant, plus <code>.context</code> (<em>heritage-catalog</em>) to guide human translators, plus a <code>.machine-translate: \"Never\"</code> policy. A conformant implementation must not auto-translate the title or the provenance narrative.</p>"
        }
      },

