      {
        "template": "Artifact",
        "fields": {
          "Title": "Letter from Private Cartwright to his sister",
          "Accession Number": "RHS.2023.011",
          "Photos": [
            {"filename": "item11_letter.jpg", "slot": 1, "caption": "Overview", "is_primary": true}
          ],
          "Object Type": "Document",
          "Date Made": "1917-09-18",
          "Materials": ["Paper", "Ink"],
          "Origin": "Cartwright Family Home",
          "Height": 25.5,
          "Width": 20.0,
          "Functional": false,
          "Popularity": 70,
          "Donor": "Helen Cartwright",
          "Accession Date": "2023-06-20",
          "Provenance": {
            ".machine-translate": "Never",
            ".en": "<p>Written by Private James Cartwright from a training camp in September 1917, three weeks before his regiment shipped overseas. Addressed to his younger sister Evelyn. Kept by Evelyn until her death in 1991, then held by her daughter Helen, who donated the letter with a transcription.</p><p>Helen's accompanying note: \"Jim never came home. Evvie kept this letter in the drawer next to her bed for seventy-four years. I want it somewhere safe now.\"</p>"
          },
          "Reference Scan": {
            "url": "https://example.org/scans/cartwright-letter-1917.pdf",
            "provider": "example.org",
            "filename": "cartwright-letter-1917.pdf"
          },
          "Notes": "<p>The <em>Provenance</em> field is marked <code>.machine-translate: \"Never\"</code>. The family's phrasing (\"Jim never came home\") is a historical quotation in the donor's own words; auto-translation would produce plausible-looking but false paraphrases. Conformant renderers display the primary-locale variant even when the viewer's locale is absent.</p>"
        }
      },

